# Rust backend

- Commands are thin: validate → call engine/db/media → map errors.
- Media: `std::process::Command` with separate args; parse `yt-dlp -J` JSON.
- Engine owns job lifecycle and progress events (`download-progress`, `download-finished`, `download-error`).
- SQLite via a dedicated `db` module with migrations from day one.
- Prefer typed `models` with serde; return structured errors to the frontend.
- Never `shell` out; never build command lines from format! with user URLs.
